  "notes":"Build99 adds canonical Git Transaction UX over Change Transactions and the existing Guarded Commit/Checkpoint/Reversible engines. Commit cards expose branch, parent, message, paths and checkpoint evidence without raw patch persistence. Revert is full-transaction only: the runtime proves an exact contiguous base-to-applied commit span with no foreign commits, requires the applied commit to remain an ancestor of current HEAD, rejects sensitive/non-text paths, builds a combined net-diff 3-way preserve preview against current HEAD, binds a short-lived fingerprint/head-lock ticket, requires explicit human confirmation, and writes only through Guarded Commit. Partial revert is never offered as fallback. This package metadata does not authorize OTA, GitHub Release, store publication or merge to main."
